# =============================================================================
# Turnwell — environment template
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values. `.env.local` is
# git-ignored and is what `vite` / `vercel dev` read on your machine.
#
# In production, do NOT use a file — set these same variable names in the
# Vercel dashboard (Project → Settings → Environment Variables), scoped to
# the "Production" (and "Preview") environments. Vercel injects them at build
# and runtime, so the same code reads the same names everywhere; only the
# values differ per environment.
#
# ⚠️  Only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to browser code. Anything
#     without that prefix (secret keys, DB URLs) stays server-side in /api and
#     must NEVER be prefixed with VITE_.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Clerk — authentication
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# We use the Clerk *Development* instance for BOTH local dev and the Vercel
# *.vercel.app deployment, because Clerk production instances require a custom
# domain (they cannot run on vercel.app). Get these from the Clerk dashboard:
#   Clerk → your app → API keys.
# When a custom domain is added later, create a Clerk Production instance and
# put its pk_live.../sk_live... values in Vercel's Production scope — no code
# change needed, just different values for these same two variables.

# Publishable key — safe for the browser (starts with pk_test_ in dev).
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Secret key — server-side ONLY, used by /api to verify session tokens.
# Never expose this to the client; never prefix with VITE_.
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Neon — Postgres database
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two isolated Neon branches keep experiments off real clinical data:
#   • local  -> the `dev` branch
#   • Vercel -> the `main` branch  (set in Vercel Production scope)
# Get the connection strings from the Neon dashboard: select the branch, then
# "Connection Details". Neon gives a *pooled* and a *direct* (unpooled) string.

# Pooled connection — used by the app at runtime via @neondatabase/serverless.
# (Neon pooled host contains "-pooler".) Keep ?sslmode=require.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# Direct (unpooled) connection — used by drizzle-kit for migrations, which
# need a single non-pooled session. Same DB, host WITHOUT "-pooler".
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# App config (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL the frontend uses to reach the API. Leave blank for same-origin
# (the default with `vercel dev` and on Vercel — /api is served alongside the
# app). Only set this if you ever run the API on a different host.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=
